WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.630
Principal's Office

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.880
The Harekaze has mutinied?!

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:10.840
Yes. When the Harekaze arrived late
at the designated meeting place,

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.510
they suddenly attacked
the instructor ship Sarushima, and sank it.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.810
Why would they do that?!

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.140
The Sarushima's captain, Instructor Furushou
hasn't regained consciousness,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.900
so we don't have any details yet.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.780
<i>A student ship has mutinied
and attacked the Sarushima.</i>

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.030
<i>The Sarushima sank,
but the captain and crew survived.</i>

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.040
Why are they calling it mutiny?
The Sarushima attacked us first!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.380
Don't ask me!

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.130
There's no point yelling at Ms. Shiretoko.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.010
Sorry, sorry.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.760
B-But I wonder why it sank.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.510
Even though it was a dummy shell.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.930
Maybe this is part of a training exercise?

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.730
Would a ship sink as part of training?

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.770
So they sunk it deliberately?

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.440
By chance, we might have stumbled
onto the Sarushima's dark secret!

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.110
Here we go again.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.240
We were just late.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.570
"You guys saw it!"

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.570
"We didn't see anything!"

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.870
- "We can't let you live anymore!"
- Boom!

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:23.960
"They got away. We'll take our secret
with us to Davy Jones' locker!"

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.960
That's all your fantasy.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:29.710
Anyway, Ms. Nosa, does that tablet
have a communication signal?

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.470
Don't worry.
I turned it off at the captain's order.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.970
It's kind of inconvenient
we can't use telecommunication equipment.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.470
It would be a pain if they found us now,
so it can't be helped.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:46.980
Sorry. I know it's hard, but only until we reach
the next rendezvous point, Torishima's coast.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.230
O-Our location-based beacon is shut off.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.860
W-We're wanted by the authorities, aren't we?

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.490
We just became high school students,
but they're branding us as criminals.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.370
It's a lie!
Someone tell me it's a lie!

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.370
It's... It's...

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.750
Is something wrong, Ms. Tateishi?

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:08.500
A lie.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.000
Th-Thank you for saying that.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.880
- You can call me Rin!
- Rin.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.020
JR Yokosuka Station

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.270
Suwa Grand Shrine

00:03:55.270 --> 00:04:01.910
Suwa God

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.820
Mashiro! You'll fall down if you run!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.910
I'm fine!

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:07.950
Mom! Sis! Hurry up!

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.660
- Hurry!
- Wait, Mashiro!

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:15.210
A long time ago, Yokosuka
had a lot of land like this, right Mom?

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.760
Yes. I think you learned about it at school,
but after the Russo-Japanese war,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.680
methane hydrate mining
began Japan's slide into land subsidence.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.300
Suwa Grand Shrine

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.560
For the submerged urban areas,
a giant floating ship was constructed,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.310
which became floating cities,
spurring on seaborne development.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.190
And that's how Japan
became a maritime nation, right?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.240
Most of the ships that were built
for the military were put to civilian use,

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.280
and as a symbol
that they wouldn't be used for war,

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.080
women became the captains.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.080
That was the beginning of the Blue Mermaids.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.830
Right, Mashimo-sis?

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.960
And the captain of the first ship...

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.170
...was your great-grandmother.

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:06.760
After that, each generation of Munetani women
became Blue Mermaids.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.010
Including me.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:14.730
But my next voyage will be the last.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:15.900
What?!

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:22.490
After that, I'm going to become
a Blue Mermaid instructor.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:26.410
I want to raise girls who live on the sea,

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.370
and become resourceful and refreshing,
just like this vast ocean.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:34.250
I want to become a girl like that!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.750
I'm going to go to the school
where you teach, Mom!

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.670
M-Me too!

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.550
I'm gonna go to that school, too!

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.170
I'm gonna go!

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.630
I look forward to it.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:02.530
<i>When I think about it,
I was always unlucky from then on.</i>

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.530
<i>My luck was always bad.</i>

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.700
<i>And now, on my maiden voyage...</i>

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.410
<i>...I'm so unlucky.</i>

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.330
This is terrible.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.460
We'd better make emergency repairs
on the aft deck.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.710
This is a big mess.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.090
1000% totally cool!

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.680
Mimi is infatuated with Ms. Noma.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.760
Ms. Tohmatsu, if you have free time,
please help us!

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.930
Macchi!

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.680
She's head over heels.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.690
I wish I could send the photo
I took with Macchi to my little sister.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:42.320
But we can't send anything
on our phones right now.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.940
Hime, Momo, Mimi, good work.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.450
What's the damage situation?

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:51.320
As you can see, we need to make
emergency repairs, Captain.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.330
Got it. I'll help you with it later.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.450
The captain's really busy, huh?

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.840
Maron, how are things?

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.340
Thanks to going full speed,
we have to do a complete overhaul!

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.680
- You really overworked it.
- Yeah!

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:11.720
Sorry, Kuro.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:15.720
Don't be so familiar.
Would you please call me "Ms. Kuroki"?

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.680
Got it, Kuro!

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.480
She doesn't get it at all.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.150
And this is our captain?

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.440
Hikari, are you okay?

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.740
Runa and Sora, were you injured at all?

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.450
You remembered our names already?!
Amazing!

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.830
She's our captain after all.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:37.290
So no one else is hurt?

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.080
No.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:41.460
Thank goodness.
I never imagined this would happen.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.590
"A bolt from the heavens."

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.250
I wonder what to do next.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.090
"The wise are not doubtful.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:51.340
The compassionate are not distressed.
The courageous are not fearful."

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.970
<i>Captain, please return
to the bridge immediately!</i>

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.230
Sorry to make you wait!

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.560
What's the damage?

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.280
The aft deck is in shambles,
we have one depth charge left,

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.860
we're out of torpedoes,
and the engine room needs an overhaul.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.370
How cute!

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.910
Don't take pictures!
Record the damage report!

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.910
Have we heard from the school?

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.040
No.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:23.330
I bet they abandoned us.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.750
They could be confirming the truth right now.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:31.510
W-We should take refuge ten miles
off the coast of Torishima, right?

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:36.720
Yeah. They're accusing us of mutiny
and attacking the Sarushima,

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.350
but we have to explain the truth.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:41.980
Maybe they'll capture us
when we arrive at the rendezvous point.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.310
"Why did you attack the Sarushima?!"

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:47.570
"We didn't! The Sarushima attacked us first!"

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.190
"Don't lie!"

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:51.070
You don't think they'll believe us?

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.910
But we have no intention of mutinying.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:59.200
We can't keep running away like this,
so let's go to the nearest port, captain.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:04.120
Ok, good point. If we go to a port,
I'm sure they won't attack us.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.460
Rin, how long would it take us
to get to Yokosuka?

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.210
Maybe 38 hours at cruising speed.

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:15.300
Sheesh, I can't believe they put me
in a class like this. I'm so unlucky.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.180
What do you mean, "a class like this?"

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:21.850
Sure, students who passed with
the lowest scores were put in the Harekaze,

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.100
but that includes you!

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:28.770
Don't put me in the same boat as you!
I'm sure I aced the entrance exam,

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.480
but I was off by one row when I filled it in.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.530
That really is unlucky.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:38.240
Shut up!

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:44.210
I-I see. I passed, but it was a miracle.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:48.170
Coincidentally, what I studied
was on the test. I didn't think I'd be captain.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:51.460
And this one has outstanding luck.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.300
Aye.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:57.800
Birds.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:01.810
At a time like this, I wish we could
fly back to school like that.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:06.560
I wonder if you can make a flying ship
without hydrogen or helium?

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:09.810
Only in your imagination.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.150
Ridiculous.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:16.320
<i>Everyone, it's time to eat!</i>

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.200
On today's menu is...

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.410
Harekaze curry!

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.710
Curry?

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.000
Today is Friday, huh?

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.460
Curry!

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.590
Alright, let's go eat in shifts.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:34.630
Aye!

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:37.090
I wonder what our ship's curry is like!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.590
A bath or curry. Which one should I do first?!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:40.970
Curry, right?

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:42.470
- Curry!
- Curry, of course

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:45.600
Ms. Munetani, would you like
to get some curry together?

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.480
Kuro is going with Maron!

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.440
60 degrees to starboard,
distance 30,000 meters,

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.990
the battleship approaching is...

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.110
<i>Admiral Spee!</i>

00:10:58.610 --> 00:10:59.740
Admiral Spee?!

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.740
It's a German exchange student ship.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:03.910
For now, all hands to your station!

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:04.870
All hands to your station!

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.250
It's approaching at a speed of 20 knots.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.880
Have they found us?

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.250
Looks like it.

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:14.500
Spee is rotating its main armament!

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:16.260
They're going to fire?!

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.050
No questions asked, huh?

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:19.260
Ms. Noma! Raise the white flag!

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.760
Spee has fired their cannon!

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:24.890
Why?

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.520
We have to stop the engine, too!

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.390
I'm sure raising the white flag alone
doesn't mean surrender.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.650
But we're going to escape, right?

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:36.110
Y-Yeah! Turn 180 degrees, full rudder!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.110
Full speed!

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.200
Full rudder!

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:41.070
Impact!

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:57.260
<i>Spee has begun accelerating!</i>

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:58.380
It's pursuing us!

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.380
Let's hurry and get away!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.810
Spee: standard water
displacement 12,100 tons.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:10.230
Maximum speed 28.5 knots.
28 cm main armaments. Six cannons.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:14.810
Eight 15 cm secondary armaments.
Eight torpedo tubes. 160 mm thick hull.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.280
It's known as a small battleship,

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:20.780
however, it's the size of a cruiser
with the firepower of a smaller warship.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:21.740
<i>Impact!</i>

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:26.870
Th-The maximum range of its main armament
is about 36,000 meters,

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:31.210
with a 300 kilo shell
and possible firing rate of 2.5 rounds a minute.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.960
If even one hits us, we'll sink instantly.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:38.210
Even its 15 cm secondary battery
is stronger than our main.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.420
We're way outclassed
by their firepower and armor.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.470
The only thing we have on them
is speed and maneuverability.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:48.720
If we keep going at full-power,
we'll definitely break down!

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.390
Can we fire a torpedo to stop them?

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:52.600
- We're out!
- Oh, that's right!

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.270
How about our firepower?

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:55.860
70 and 5.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.440
You mean 7,000 and 50 mm?

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.610
What's the Spee's broadside armor?

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.190
80 mm.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.070
30.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:02.740
So we can get through it at 3,000 meters?

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:05.120
They're actually communicating properly!

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.990
- So that's the ability of a captain?
- Of course not!

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.370
Maron! How fast can we keep going?!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:13.120
Up to fourth battle speed!

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.250
Fourth battle speed... 27 knots.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.590
That's about the same
as their top battle speed.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:20.710
What should we do?

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.170
Round and round.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:24.380
Round and round.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.760
Rin, hard left rudder!

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:30.810
- H-Hard left rudder!
- What do you intend to do?!

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.350
- Left rudder, 30 degrees!
- We'll hide in the smoke!

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:44.360
Back! Hard right rudder!

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.910
Back! Hard right rudder!

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.530
Right rudder, 30 degrees!

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:50.790
If they hit us even once, we're doomed.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:54.000
All we can do is leverage our speed
and maneuverability to keep running around.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.920
Maron! Make the engine combust unevenly!

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.130
<i>Aye-aye, Captain!</i>

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.300
You want to make a smokescreen, right?

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.510
<i>We're running around,</i>

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.760
which will put a strain on the engine,
but I'm counting on you!

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.300
"I'm counting on you?"

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.890
We gotta do what we gotta do!

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.890
Rin, make our course irregular,
and also our speed, if possible!

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:15.100
But without letting our speed drop too much!

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:18.100
The only way to stop them
is by using live ammo!

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:31.620
Battle, left cannon. 30 degrees, Spee.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.330
What are you talking about?!
This will end up just like the Sarushima!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:39.500
We'll use live ammo to pierce them
with a screw shot. That should stop them.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.840
If we take that step, it really will be mutiny!

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:45.220
At this rate, people will get hurt.

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:02.480
OFF / ARM
CAUTION, FIRE

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.110
Unlocking live ammo!

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:08.990
Good.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.490
Locked and loaded.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:13.450
Ready to fire!

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.870
What should the distance be for a screw shot?

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:20.540
The speed of the shell decreases rapidly
underwater, so it's impossible!

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.000
There are underwater shells, aren't there?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:25.010
That's only for cruisers and higher,
so we're not equipped with them.

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:28.170
I heard that even normal shells
can be shot underwater.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:32.970
In theory, a 12.7 cm shell's
accumulated distance is about 10 m underwater,

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:36.020
so if the idea is to pierce broadside armor...

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:39.060
...please get us within 3,000 meters.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:41.770
Get us within 3,000 m while maintaining
a figure eight pattern!

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.150
Get closer to them?! I'm scared!

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:45.610
What are you saying?!

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.780
I'm saying that I'm scared!

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.660
Okay. Understood.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.540
What are you doing?!

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:00.460
- Please get closer to them.
- I don't want to!

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:01.920
- Take this seriously!
- It's dark!

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:08.800
Distance 4,000 meters.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.010
3,800.

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:12.930
3,600.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:19.350
<i>A small craft is approaching us
from the Admiral Spee!</i>

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:31.400
<i>The pilot of the small craft fell into the sea!</i>

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.280
They're attacking their comrade?!

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:33.780
Why?!

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:37.790
"I can't follow your orders, Captain!
I can't attack the Harekaze!"

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.700
"What?! You disobey your captain?!"

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:42.670
"I'm leaving this crummy ship!"

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.630
You don't have to act out your imagination!

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:47.670
To me, fiction is truer than non-fiction.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:49.130
With a diameter of 700 meters
and an angular velocity of 20 knots,

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.130
Shiro.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:52.550
- Please call me Ms. Munetani or Dep—
- Can I leave this to you?

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.050
Distract that German ship!

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:57.970
Coco, call our medic, Ms. Minami to the deck!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:58.680
What are you...

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.480
Don't tell me.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.560
Why would you help the enemy?!

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:04.440
She's not the enemy.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.820
Comrades at sea are all family.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.070
I'll be back.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:14.950
Akeno Misaki

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.170
The captain went to rescue
the girl who fell in?!

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:30.510
Get us to within 3,000 meters of them.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.680
Distance 3,200 meters.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:39.930
3,100.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.390
Fire! Fire! Fire!

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.190
Second cannon right, commence firing!

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:56.990
We hit the target!

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:59.240
<i>The Spee is decelerating!</i>

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.950
We did it!

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.200
Hard left rudder!

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.120
Fourth battle speed, steady as she goes!

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.210
Hard left rudder!

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:10.590
She's quite prompt when we're escaping.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.230
Are you okay?! Hang in there!

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.620
It's all right. You're alive.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:52.420
- She's heavy.
- Please take care of her.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:18:59.340
Shiro.

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:02.600
Thank you.

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.180
I just followed orders.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.980
Full battle speed. Let's leave this area.

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:10.730
<i>Maron! I'm counting on you.</i>

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.030
She'll destroy us!

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.240
For real.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:29.620
What should we do now?

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.970
I can't look nervous!

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:41.140
Because I'm the captain!

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:44.470
Right, Moka?

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:50.810
Ms. Minami?

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:53.900
Captain.

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:54.940
How is she?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.860
No external injuries.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:58.190
Her brainwaves are normal, too.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.570
All we can do is wait for her
to regain consciousness.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.120
I see.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.330
Thank you.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.370
I can watch her,
so please go eat, Ms. Minami.

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:10.210
A million thanks.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.850
I'm all sweaty.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.520
I finally feel refreshed.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:31.690
I really thought the engine was going to blow.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:35.320
Now it's time for the long-awaited curry!

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:38.440
Okay, eat up!

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:40.950
This is 120% seriously delicious!

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.240
So this is Harekaze curry!

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.950
We finally get to eat it!

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.910
- It's curry today?
- Yeah, because it's Friday.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.200
Yummy!

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.120
It's sweet, but also has a rich flavor!

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:55.210
That's because the secret ingredient
is blueberry jam.

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.210
Delicious!

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.500
Yeah, it is delicious!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:00.300
- We did it!
- Yeah, we did it!

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:05.350
I'll bring some to Macchi, too.

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:07.390
Who is she calling "Macchi"?!

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.180
Is our Art Director a fan of Kuro?

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.100
What?!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:17.110
Recycle         Trash

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:14.350
Huh? Where's Ms. Munetani?

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:17.110
I don't know. Probably on the bridge.

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:24.450
Ms. Munetani, good work.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:25.990
I brought you some curry.

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:27.870
Oh, thank you.

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:31.500
Don't work too hard.

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:39.420
A message?

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:43.300
I'm so unlucky.

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:49.100
<i>Captain! Please come
to the bridge immediately!</i>

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:53.060
Shiro, what's wrong?

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:55.270
- We got an emergency distress call!
- From where?

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.150
From the Musashi!

00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:58.440
The Musashi!

00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:01.440
<i>This is the Musashi... This is the Musashi...</i>

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:05.530
Moka?! It's me, Akeno!
What's wrong?! Did something happen?!

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:09.200
<i>We have an emergency...
Please send help at once...</i>

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:14.080
<i>We're northwest of Asuncion Island.
Northwest of Asuncion Island.</i>

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:16.370
<i>Send help at once...</i>

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:18.590
Send help at once!

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:24.970
Episode 2: In a Pinch During the Pursuit!
